# Large STAT cache — 2.4 GB, auto-fetched by 01_stat/02_fetch/stat_fetch.py (all of
# stat_fetch/data/ is fetch-stage cache/checkpoints; stat_filter/data/ holds
# the actual final outputs — runs.tsv etc. — and stays tracked)
01_stat/02_fetch/data/*
!01_stat/02_fetch/data/manifest.tsv

# Intermediate confirmed-run caches — regeneratable from stat_cache
01_stat/03_filter/data/*_confirmed.json

# Large species distribution table (38k rows)
01_stat/03_filter/data/*_species_dist.tsv

# Reference DB source files — auto-downloaded by 01_stat/01_build/stat_build.py
01_stat/01_build/data/phi-base_current.csv
01_stat/01_build/data/ictv_vmr.xlsx

# meta_search.py raw API response caches — regeneratable
02_literature/01_search/data/bp_cache.json
02_literature/01_search/data/bs_cache.json
02_literature/01_search/data/serper_cache.json

# meta_text.py: manually-downloaded copyrighted journal PDFs (715MB+, and not
# ours to redistribute) — never committed. Its .bak sibling is working-copy
# cruft, also excluded.
02_literature/02_text/data/manual_pdfs/
02_literature/02_text/data/text_cache.jsonl.bak

# The repo is for code (+ small figures/manifests to discuss results), not
# data — 2026-08-31 policy, purged from history at the same time. These are
# all locally regeneratable (or synced to Setonix directly, outside git) —
# see the module docstrings/READMEs for how each is produced.
02_literature/01_search/data/bioprojects.json
02_literature/01_search/data/biosamples.json
02_literature/02_text/data/text_cache.jsonl
02_literature/03_classify/data/samples.tsv
02_literature/03_classify/data/classify_cache.jsonl
02_literature/03_classify/data/host_disambig_cache.jsonl
01_stat/01_build/data/phibase_db.json
01_stat/03_filter/data/runs.tsv
01_stat/03_filter/figures/scatter_data.tsv

# legacy/ dirs (superseded scripts + their outputs, kept on disk for local
# reference only) — excluded from the repo entirely rather than picking
# through individual files; simpler, and none of it is needed anywhere
# downstream (nothing reads from legacy/, matching kraken/legacy/ having been
# fully wiped rather than kept at all — see 03_kraken/README.md "History").

# Log history dirs + .latest symlinks are now TRACKED (transparency — Leon's
# call 2026-09-01: full run history should be visible in the repo, not just
# code). Do not re-add exclusions for logs/history/ or logs/*.latest here.

# Stray BUSCO container job logs that end up at repo root on Setonix
/busco_*.log
busco_downloads/

# Kraken2 classify cache — large, regeneratable on Setonix
03_kraken/04_assign/data/kraken_cache*.jsonl
03_kraken/04_assign/data/kraken_cache*.txt
# every reports dir is data: reports/ is the current DB's, reports_db_v2/ the baseline
03_kraken/04_assign/data/reports*/
# ad-hoc classification analyses run from 03_kraken/slurm/ (db_v2-vs-v3 comparison,
# the Phakopsora counterfactual): reports and extracted reads, both regenerable
03_kraken/04_assign/data/compare_v2v3/
03_kraken/04_assign/data/phak_cf/

# Old output/ directory — local pipeline data, all superseded by module layout
/output/

# Claude Code project settings
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Colleague correspondence / external documents
kristina/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env

# Kraken2 large files (reproducible, not tracked)
03_kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/indices/
03_kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/quant/
03_kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/reads/
03_kraken/utilities/pilot/kallisto/refs/
